From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rnsbox <rnsbox@localhost>
Date: Thu, 16 Oct 2026 21:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] sg200x-arm64: cap &sd at 25 MHz, align the u-boot
 defconfigs with the vendor

The board bring-up died at the u-boot prompt: loadenvcmd (no "mmc dev")
read the boot FAT fine, but both sdboot and sdbootauto died with
"Can't set block device" right after "mmc dev 0". Root cause chain:

  - the arm64 board dts inherited soph_base.dtsi's &sd verbatim - no
    max-frequency, so the card trains to 50 MHz HS ("Bus Speed: 50000000
    Mode: SD High Speed (50MHz)" in the boot log). Every vendor sg200x
    board dir caps &sd at 25 MHz (50 is commented out as unstable), and
    the RV sg2000_duomodule01_sd dir shipped the 25 MHz cap from day one
    - only the two arm64 dirs missed it;
  - the sdboot/sdbootauto env run "mmc dev 0" before fatloading
    boot.sd, and cmd/mmc.c forces a FULL re-init there. A re-handshake
    at 50 MHz on these pads desyncs the card; the next part_init inside
    fatload reads garbage, finds no partition table, falls back to the
    whole device, and the FAT probe on the MBR fails -> "Can't set
    block device". The same read via an already-initialized link
    (loadenvcmd) works, which is why uEnv.txt handling looked healthy.

Cap &sd at 25 MHz on both arm64 boards, and while in here align the
u-boot defconfigs with the vendor ARM64 reference
(sg2002_licheea53nano_sd): explicit CONFIG_DM_MMC/CONFIG_MMC,
CONFIG_CMD_CVI_SD_UPDATE, CONFIG_ENV_IS_NOWHERE.
---
diff --git a/build/boards/sg200x/sg2000_duo01evb_arm64_sd/dts_arm64/sg2000_duo01evb_arm64_sd.dts b/build/boards/sg200x/sg2000_duo01evb_arm64_sd/dts_arm64/sg2000_duo01evb_arm64_sd.dts
index 74ee3a2..f3cd8a2 100644
--- a/build/boards/sg200x/sg2000_duo01evb_arm64_sd/dts_arm64/sg2000_duo01evb_arm64_sd.dts
+++ b/build/boards/sg200x/sg2000_duo01evb_arm64_sd/dts_arm64/sg2000_duo01evb_arm64_sd.dts
@@ -35,3 +35,14 @@
 / {
 	model = "Milk-V Duo Module 01 Evaluation Board (ARM64)";
 };
+
+// RNSBox: cap the SD interface at 25 MHz. The vendor sg200x board dirs
+// all do (and so does the RV sg2000_duomodule01_sd dir): these pads are
+// only 25 MHz-stable. Without the cap the card trains to 50 MHz HS, and
+// the sdboot env's forced re-init ("mmc dev") desyncs it - the following
+// fatload's part_init reads garbage and every boot dies with
+// "Can't set block device" at the soph# prompt.
+&sd {
+	min-frequency = <400000>; // 400Khz
+	max-frequency = <25000000>; // 25Mhz
+};
diff --git a/build/boards/sg200x/sg2000_duo01evb_arm64_sd/u-boot/sg2000_duo01evb_arm64_sd_defconfig b/build/boards/sg200x/sg2000_duo01evb_arm64_sd/u-boot/sg2000_duo01evb_arm64_sd_defconfig
index 0408b74..6ea6eda 100644
--- a/build/boards/sg200x/sg2000_duo01evb_arm64_sd/u-boot/sg2000_duo01evb_arm64_sd_defconfig
+++ b/build/boards/sg200x/sg2000_duo01evb_arm64_sd/u-boot/sg2000_duo01evb_arm64_sd_defconfig
@@ -48,3 +48,10 @@ CONFIG_BMP_32BPP=y
 CONFIG_LZ4=y
 CONFIG_LZMA=y
 # CONFIG_TOOLS_LIBCRYPTO is not set
+# RNSBox: align with the vendor ARM64 reference (sg2002_licheea53nano_sd):
+# explicit MMC driver-model wiring, the cvi_sd_update command, and the
+# env-in-nowhere storage the SD-only boot actually uses.
+CONFIG_DM_MMC=y
+CONFIG_MMC=y
+CONFIG_CMD_CVI_SD_UPDATE=y
+CONFIG_ENV_IS_NOWHERE=y
diff --git a/build/boards/sg200x/sg2002_duo_arm64_sd/dts_arm64/sg2002_duo_arm64_sd.dts b/build/boards/sg200x/sg2002_duo_arm64_sd/dts_arm64/sg2002_duo_arm64_sd.dts
index f7126cd..15622bf 100644
--- a/build/boards/sg200x/sg2002_duo_arm64_sd/dts_arm64/sg2002_duo_arm64_sd.dts
+++ b/build/boards/sg200x/sg2002_duo_arm64_sd/dts_arm64/sg2002_duo_arm64_sd.dts
@@ -38,3 +38,14 @@
 / {
 	model = "Milk-V Duo (SG2002, ARM64)";
 };
+
+// RNSBox: cap the SD interface at 25 MHz. The vendor sg200x board dirs
+// all do (and so does the RV sg2000_duomodule01_sd dir): these pads are
+// only 25 MHz-stable. Without the cap the card trains to 50 MHz HS, and
+// the sdboot env's forced re-init ("mmc dev") desyncs it - the following
+// fatload's part_init reads garbage and every boot dies with
+// "Can't set block device" at the soph# prompt.
+&sd {
+	min-frequency = <400000>; // 400Khz
+	max-frequency = <25000000>; // 25Mhz
+};
diff --git a/build/boards/sg200x/sg2002_duo_arm64_sd/u-boot/sg2002_duo_arm64_sd_defconfig b/build/boards/sg200x/sg2002_duo_arm64_sd/u-boot/sg2002_duo_arm64_sd_defconfig
index 0408b74..6ea6eda 100644
--- a/build/boards/sg200x/sg2002_duo_arm64_sd/u-boot/sg2002_duo_arm64_sd_defconfig
+++ b/build/boards/sg200x/sg2002_duo_arm64_sd/u-boot/sg2002_duo_arm64_sd_defconfig
@@ -48,3 +48,10 @@ CONFIG_BMP_32BPP=y
 CONFIG_LZ4=y
 CONFIG_LZMA=y
 # CONFIG_TOOLS_LIBCRYPTO is not set
+# RNSBox: align with the vendor ARM64 reference (sg2002_licheea53nano_sd):
+# explicit MMC driver-model wiring, the cvi_sd_update command, and the
+# env-in-nowhere storage the SD-only boot actually uses.
+CONFIG_DM_MMC=y
+CONFIG_MMC=y
+CONFIG_CMD_CVI_SD_UPDATE=y
+CONFIG_ENV_IS_NOWHERE=y
2.43.0

